{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795626232,"nonce":"zj/nZ9FI0ksoCedLI/s8TW1tPL8=","title":"Code editor rows are unevenly spaced when the line height is not a whole number","message":"The editable and read-only code widgets give each line a row of `font_size * line_height` pixels. At the default line height of 1.5, an odd font size gives a half pixel: 13 gives 19.5. Layout rounds positions to whole logical pixels, so the rows alternate.\n\nMeasured headless at font size 13: the tops of rows 1 to 6 are 18, 38, 57, 77, 96, 116, gaps of 20, 19, 20, 19, 20. Gutter and code agree, so they stay aligned with each other. On a 2x display the uneven gap is easy to see; it shows in the website's code editor preview, and did so before cn::code_editor.\n\nProposed: compute the line height in px in one place and round it to a whole pixel (or to a whole device pixel), and use that value for rows, gutter, caret, selection, hit testing and scroll-into-view. Those compute `font_size * line_height` separately today, so changing the rows alone would let the caret drift.","files":null}]}